# Hand-authored bark sources: one folder per source, each holding a diffuse
# (sRGB), an arm and a 16-bit disp map. Tileable on both axes, authored with the
# trunk running up the image. No normal map — tree-forge derives it from the
# composited height. See ../../../../docs/tree-forge.md.
#
# Large binaries, kept out of git the way /assets/ is. With no source here the
# forge generates its bark instead, so a fresh clone still builds. This rule
# keeps the file itself tracked so the folder survives that clone.
*
!.gitignore
